# Brooklyn99 — Recon & Priv Esc
Difficulty: easy
Tools: nmap & hydra & GTFObin
Vulnerability: Misconfigured sudo Permisions & Weak Password Implementation & Allowing Anonymous User on FTP

What I was given: A website and a set of flags to recover
What worked: Using hydra to bruteforce a user password on ssh
Steps: 
  1. Using nmap to see the open ports: SSH, FTP & HTTP
  2. Log in FTP as anonymous
  3. Search the FTP server for clues which reveals a note named 'note_to_jake.txt' which suggest a user with name "jake" with weak password implementation
  4. Use hydra to bruteforce the login for SSH
  5. Log in to the SSH and check allowed commands on sudo (command 'less' does not need a password)
  6. Use "less" on any file and input !/bin/bash and press enter to spawn the root shell
  7. Enumerate the place which will uncover the USER flag located in 'holt/user.txt' andthe ROOT flag located in '/root/root.txt'
  8. Submit the given flags
Things I learned: 
  1. Basic priv esc using misconfigured sudo permisions
  2. Exploiting FTP misconfiguration using an anonymous account
  3. Using hydra to bruteforce a weak account password
